No.  It is not an accident that Alpha binaries on True/64 (or whatever
they call it currently) and Linux are so similar, but is due to a lot
of work and support of Digital in the development of Alpha Linux.

Now how much work has Microsoft invested in order to make sure Linux
and Windows binaries are compatible?  I would like to say "none", but
that would be inaccurate.  The fact is that Microsoft has invested a
*lot* of work to make sure that Windows is *incompatible* with
whatever other platform available.


