Check this: 
You need to set -D_GNU_SOURCE when compiling, otherwise utmpx has no
e_termination or e_exit member. GLIBC funnies. 

Concerning "ut_syslen": "configure" checks for ut_syslen in utmpx and
#defines HAVE_SYSLEN_IN_UTMPX, and its use is guarded by an #ifdef/endif
bracket within the source. But as of ssh-1.2.26 theres an extra access
to ut_syslen outside such a bracket and thus the compiler bailes out.
Here's a patch against login.c from ssh-1.2.26, maybe this error slipped
into wtmp.c of ssh-2.

--- login.c.orig        Sat May 29 12:39:42 1999
+++ login.c     Sat May 29 12:40:00 1999
@@ -434,7 +434,6 @@
     ux.ut_session = pid;
     strncpy(ux.ut_host, host, sizeof(ux.ut_host));
     ux.ut_host[sizeof(ux.ut_host) - 1] = 0;
-    ux.ut_syslen = strlen(ux.ut_host);
 #ifdef HAVE_SYSLEN_IN_UTMPX
     ux.ut_syslen = strlen(ux.ut_host);
 #endif

