Just to add my little opinion.  I spent some time trying to decide what to get
for a powerful home machine and have come to the following conclusion.

I can only compare machines on published benchmarks and opinions because I
can't get my hands on an alpha machine (despite there being a Cray in the next
room).  Also looking closely at CPU prices (UK) I find that a 400 Mhz PII is
200 pounds compared to 350 for that extra 50 Mhz.  PII has basically same
performance as PIII unless you can use the fp SIMD stuff.  So the upshot is
that for the price of an Alpha box with moderate spec (3.4 G IDE, 64Mb RAM) I
can build a dual 400 PII system with UW SCSI and 128Mb RAM.  This ought to
give me more oomph than either Alpha or a 500Mhz PIII.  Of course if the 21264
drops into the realm of the affordable I will cram that into the same machine
and maybe network the 2 motherboards for a small cluster.

If only there was an easy way to create multiprocessor systems with all those
cheap(ish) ARMs, K6s, etc.

