I've experenced this and found a solution. You must disable the
fontserver (xfs) and in the /etc/XF86Config file you must change the
font path from "unix/:-1" to the absolute paths to the fonts like this.

    FontPath  
"/usr/lib/X11/fonts/misc:unscaled,/usr/lib/X11/fonts/75dpi:unscaled,/usr/lib/X11/fonts/Speedo,/usr/lib/X11/fonts/Type1,/usr/lib/X11/fonts/misc,/usr/lib/X11/fonts/75dpi,/usr/lib/X11/fonts/URW"

This was resolved on the AXP list a few days ago. 

Peter

