What surprised me the most that g++ on alpha
will do:

sizeof(bool) == 8

64 bits used, to store just a single one!

Also ofcourse, sizeof(long) == sizeof(void *) == 8.

Some quick-n-dirty programmers use ints to hold
ptr values though, and that's a real pain.

However, most linux packages are now 64bit safe.
Debian/alpha is pretty complete when it comes
to available packages.
 
