On Wed, 26 May 1999 14:33:25 GMT, Dang H. Nguyen <dang@cadif.cornell.edu> wrote:
>Hello,
>My Debian 2.1 Multia machine keeps getting its clock set forward to
>year 2019 everytime I turn it off and leave it for about a day. This
>happens even with a new nvram battery.
>Anyone have similar problem? Fix?
>Dang.

I had a similar problem; it was resolved by telling Linux the system clock
was in ARC format.

Here's the content of the /etc/sysconfig/clock file :
	UTC=false
	ARC=true

This file is from a LX164 running Redhat 5.1. I'm not so sure for
Debian systems...

Francois.



