In article <look-0905992211190001@hse-tor-ppp22684.sympatico.ca>,
look@bottom.net (Patrick West) wrote:
> I was thinking of getting a multia, so I went over to the cpumicromart web page.
> they have two models VX40A-N2 and VX40A-N3.
> I found out that the N means it doesn't come with a floppy but what does
> the last number mean?
>
> Patrick
>
> --
> My Email address is patwest at snickers.org
>
From the Multia user manual:

  VX  - header code
   4  - Alpha CPU
   0  - fixed 256K cache, fixed 166MHz CPU
   A  - shipped with US power cord

   N  - no floppy
   2  - 2.5" internal disk, PCI slot, external SCSI
   3  - 3.5" internal disk, no PCI slot, no external SCSI

