Rob Stewart wrote:
> 
> When I install a 3Com 905BTX PCI ethernet card in my Alphastation 200 and
> load the 3c95x module to support it, linux complains that the 8th data byte
> is incorrect.  I've recompiled the modules, downloaded the most current code
> and compiled it, but still the data error.  This card worked fine under 5.2
> so it isn't the card.  Any ideas?

I'm sure *Linux* doesn't complain (Linux is the kernel)
*Ping* complains, because ping is proken. In 2.2, timeval consists of
two 8 byte values, and ping boldly assumes it is two ints (like it was
before). This gives the incorrect data byte and also produces unaligned
traps.

Try my patch for ping (patches netkit-base-0.11+)
  
- Alex

