Marshall G. Gates wrote:
> 
> You are correct, there was mention of a patch for gdb, but I can't find my
> copy of it anywhere.  I did not download it and apply it.  Much to my
> dismay.
> 
> Oh well.  If anyone has it, or has a link to it.  Please post it.

The problem is, that 2.0 kernels write the timeval with int (32 bit)
fields, while 2.1/2.2 kernels write seconds and usecs as long. Nobody
(me included) wants to fix gdb so that it knows both types of core
files.
I used the following hack to make gdb read kernel 2.2 core files. It
can't read cores generated by 2.0 anymore

in the gdb sources:
in bfd/elfcode.h insert 

struct timeval {
  long tv_sec;
  long tv_usec;
};
#define _STRUCT_TIMEVAL

right between the comments and #include "bfd.h"
This did the trick for me with both gdb-4.18 and 4.17

Hope this helps
- Alex



