>   I guess I was unclear.  I meant that a binary recompiler could take
>   the Alpha executable image generated by gcc and recompile and reschedule
>   the code.

  This is called "peephole optimization", and its ability to improve
code is sharply limited because it lacks high-level information about
the code it is manipulating.  The GCC back-end (and for some architec-
tures the GAS assembler) already does quite a bit of very good peephole
optimization.  The gap between GCC's and DECC's effectiveness is due to
optimizations performed further upstream at the icode levels.

