> > I've run into some problems installing redhat 5.2 or 6.0 on a
> > compaq ds20 with dual cpus and 512 MB of ram. The versions of salient
> 
> As the FAQ at www.alphalinux.org says, you can't install with the
> default kernel in Redhat 5.2. I don't know about 6.0, but it is an
> important issue. As usual, Jay has an appropriate kernel you can ftp
> from gatekeeper.
> 
> -- g

The problems are deeper than that, as I stated, no kernels worked
including the one on the alphalinux.org ftp site. Thanks in part to
Lawrence Mcyntire at Oak Ridge, I've been able to install redhat 5.2
on the ds20. So, what I'd like to do is go throuh a postmortem of my
install experiences. The initial problem that I had was that *any*
kernel would have output similar to the following on boot,

reading 172 blocks from dva0.0.0.0.0
bootstrap code read in
base = 200000, image_start = 0, image_bytes = 15800
initializing HWRPB at 2000
initializing page table at 1ff7a000
initializing machine state
setting processor affinity to primary cpu
jumping to bootstrap code

At which point the computer would appear to hang. But what was
happening was that the output of aboot was being redirected to the
serial line (thanks Lawrence). So at the console over the serial line
I was able to boot the kernel from ftp.alphalinux.org. But that's when
I ran into my next problem. I had unplugged the monitor and keyboard
which had caused me the first set of problems. After the uncompressing
kernel message, the output goes to the video card!!! So I had to use
both the serial line console and vga+ps2 keyboard console to get
through the install. 

These problems all come back to one thing... Servers should not have
any kind of video card (this system is a loaner and it came with the
card). But, the fix for the problem is;

- Better instructions for installation (the srm howto needs help)
- Redirection of the console needs to be incorporated in aboot,
  should be another option on the command line.

I know, put up or shut up. If we get more alphas I will be able to
work on these things. But I just wanted to post my experiences with
installing linux on the ds20. I'll post my experiences with redhat-6.0
in a few days. And by the way, this computer is obscenely fast, I
can't wait for the fortran compiler from DEC-compaq.

Doug



