> You need to apply the unencrypted password fix to NT. You can grab the patch
> at ftp://ftp.wpi.edu/samba/NT4_PlainPassword.reg .
This is the easy, though insecure solution, and recommended if you don't
have any security concerns.
The other solution is to enable the samba secure password feature on
your linux box, (by uncommenting the lines in your /etc/smb.conf file)
and setting up passwords/users with the 'smbadduser ntid:unixid'
feature. This latter will give you a prompt to enter a user/password on
your NT box, and your security setup will be back in good shape. The
other option transmits passwords in clear text, and can be a rather
risky manouver, especially if you are part of a large network with
TCP/IP. If you go with the second option, make sure you stop and restart
your samba server (by typing "/etc/rc.d/init.d/smb stop &&
/etc/rc.d/init.d/smb start" for Redhat). Good luck!

---Maxx

