Kai Schmidt (kai@hirvi.net) wrote:
: Hello,

: I have a little problem with one of my multia's. I got the machine two
: weeks
: ago, I installed Linux everything was ok, suddenly the machine was
: dead, no
: ping no telnet. After rebooting I was able to connect via telnet but
: after a
: few keystrokes it turned dead again. Only this time a reboot didn't
: help.

: There is no screen output I supose no video signal, nothing, the fan
: is
: still running, is this the well know'n heat death?

That is what my dead one did... boot and run for a little while, and
then lock up. If i rebooted real quick it would die in the blue screen
arc console, if it cooled off, a few minutes would go by before it died.

It just needed a new ic on the bottom of the board. Something like
a 74F623D gets replaced with a faster/lower power compatible part. 
The info will be in the heat death faq. Since I am working by memory
here, i won't even try to tell you what part to use. The one on the
bottom of my multia was actually discolored black in the middle of the
chip, and the board was overheated. All you do is take a razor blade 
and carefully cut each of the leads off of the chip and pry the chip out
and then desolder the leads afterwards, clean up the pads with solder
wick, and solder in the new part, being very careful about aligning
the part and not making any solder bridges between pins. Also static
has to be protected against. 

A bad battery will prevent even getting into the arc firmware, and you 
don't have a chance to make any keystrokes as I recall.

There could always be a different bad part or problem, but the above is
a good start.

