I got the problem solved, and here's the solution....
For some reason, the install does not work off of sunsite.auc.dk. (of
Starbuck) and it fails at the mouse detection. The other site I found
Starbuck at was 

ftp://phyppro1.phy.bnl.gov/

with the dir being -

pub/mirror/redhat-main/starbuck/alpha/

and this one really works on an FTP install.... with one *small*
problem.
It doesn't copy the vmlinux.gz from floppy to the HDD, so when you try
to reboot, it cant. The solution is to mount the boot disk and copy the
vmlinux.gz file to the HDD, during the install process (I did it during
the 'configure printer' step), and voila.... boots perfect.
Maybe this is just amazing to me because I'm delirious on Mountain Dew
right now (been up upgrading 5 kernels and doing this inst. :-D), but I
hope that helped anyone that may run into the same issue.

---Maxx



